      "seed": 964929223,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1325681961,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794897526,
      "created": 1794794897526,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 1,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "columns",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- The three problems grow along different dimensions, so each needs its own control.\n- An EA is a saved identity with assigned work and history. An EA run is one execution of that saved agent.\n- A Task in OpenPoke is a multi-step tool operation, such as Search Email. I keep that separate from EA identity.\n- The board groups the changes into discovery, context, and execution."
      },
      "name": "02 — The overload problems"
    },
