      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 2,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "diagram",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- The IA stays responsible for the conversation and delegation. Execution Agents perform the assigned work.\n- The registry, search index, vectors, execution memory, and queue use SQLite. No separate vector database is required.\n- Scheduled Triggers use the same queue as chat requests, so they share the limits.\n- EAs call Gmail and Task tools. Those external tool calls are outside the simplified diagram.\n- Source: README.md and docs/agent-optimization.md in the OpenPoke repository."
      },
      "name": "03 — Updated architecture"
    },
