    {
      "id": "gAfzljmg3YJ6AlIfLnhSw",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 8186,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 404072295,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1693837672,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794897834,
      "created": 1794794897834,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 5,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "stats",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- The queue persists jobs before dispatch. The oldest runnable work starts first, while per-EA serialization avoids concurrent state updates.\n- Each result group collects related EA outcomes. Workers may start before submissions finish, but delivery waits for the full group.\n- A failed or rejected job still counts as an outcome, so the IA can handle the group coherently.\n- Defaults also cap each initiating request at five follow-up stages and twenty EA job submissions.\n- The queue supports one backend process. Multi-process dispatch would need additional coordination."
      },
      "name": "06 — Queue and outcome delivery"
    },
    {
      "id": "bc9r1LN0FgbJ84T9GZUpD",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 9816,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1823222055,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 576954569,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794897882,
      "created": 1794794897882,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 6,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "columns",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- A timeout can occur after an external action happened but before the final result was recorded. Blind replay could duplicate that action.\n- Interrupted writes or unknown tools put the EA behind a review gate until someone inspects the original tool state and resolves the interruption.\n- Archival requires explicit completion and thirty inactive days. Pending work or approvals, active Triggers, queued/running jobs, ambiguous legacy history, and unresolved interruptions block it.\n- Stable operation keys deduplicate submissions and replies. Restart recovery resumes unexpired queued jobs.\n- The next slides show recorded evidence, with the limits of each evaluation visible."
      },
      "name": "07 — Recovery and lifecycle"
    },
