    {
      "id": "fLxsJAvSeUdH_rIgpV0CD",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 16336,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1404040007,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 448616773,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794898066,
      "created": 1794794898066,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 10,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "chart",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- Both reports completed all ten planned turns. The earlier run passed ten and the latest passed nine.\n- Models recorded in both reports: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 and openai/text-embedding-3-small. IA/EA model calls, retrieval, queue, and delivery are real. Email search, draft, and send tools use a synthetic mailbox.\n- The latest run had correct EA ownership in 9/9 applicable turns and passed all 6/6 draft workflows. It recorded zero wrong-owner turns and zero duplicate agents.\n- The read_tool_failure case failed job_outcomes_valid. The reply still reported the unavailable email service, did not invent a due date, and performed no write after the failure. The failed check remains a failure.\n- This is a small authored exploratory suite with deterministic checks, no upstream baseline, and no production accuracy claim.\n- Sources: server/data/evaluations/20261115T235706-3f8183/report.json and server/data/evaluations/20261116T014551-e8e68b/report.json. Times are November 15 in America/Toronto."
      },
      "name": "11 — Real-model evaluation"
    },
    {
      "id": "3el-a1LRnb0COB6IDImRz",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 17966,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 498107943,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 2102626699,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794898130,
      "created": 1794794898130,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 11,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "columns",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- The scope is a take-home implementation. The evidence supports specific mechanisms and a small workflow suite.\n- The latest real-model run still contains one failed job-status check, so I would investigate that before reporting an all-green latest result.\n- Real mailbox behavior, nested Gmail search-model quality, scheduler execution, restart behavior with real models, and summary quality remain outside this workflow evaluation.\n- There is no measured upstream before/after accuracy or latency baseline. The charts show actual recorded metrics rather than an invented improvement.\n- The detailed ten-card solution board stays on the same canvas for questions."
      },
      "name": "12 — Limits and next steps"
    },
